# OVL-2: asking for the numpad while the keyboard is up (the CLI is the only way in, since the
# pad's buttons all belong to the keyboard then) closes the keyboard and opens the numpad; asking
# for the keyboard again swaps back. Never both.
press guide
advance 100
tap west 60
release guide
advance 400
expect overlay showing keyboard
cli numpad-toggle
advance 100
expect overlay showing numpad
expect overlay keyboard.board numpad
cli overlay-toggle
advance 100
expect overlay showing keyboard
expect overlay keyboard.board basic
cli overlay-toggle
advance 100
expect overlay showing none
---
shifts mode Guide layers - @0
overlay none + info 1      @100
shifts mode - layers -     @100
overlay keyboard           @100
sound keyboard Open pop    @100
overlay none               @560
sound keyboard Close pop   @560
overlay keyboard           @560
sound numpad Open pop      @560
overlay none               @660
sound numpad Close pop     @660
overlay keyboard           @660
sound keyboard Open pop    @660
overlay none               @760
sound keyboard Close pop   @760
